The national identifier is optional, and the distinguishing code for the United Kingdom, including Northern Ireland is "UK".<ref name="auto">{{cite web |url=http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/trans/conventn/Distsigns.pdf |website=[[United Nations Economic Commission for Europe]] (UNECE) |title=Distinguishing signs used on vehicles in international traffic notified to the Secretary-General of the United Nations in accordance with the 1968 Convention on Road Traffic (article 45 (4)) and the 1949 Convention on Road Traffic (annex 4) |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210430214615/https://unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/trans/conventn/Distsigns.pdf |archive-date=30 April 2021}}</ref> Number plates including the code are valid in countries party to the [[Vienna Convention on Road Traffic]] if displayed on its own or together with the [[Flag of the United Kingdom|Union Jack]]. The "UK" code replaced the previous "GB" code from 28 September 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://treaties.un.org/doc/Publication/CN/2021/CN.207.2021-Eng.pdf|title=Convention on Road Traffic Vienna, 8 November 1968: UNITED KINGDOM OF GREAT BRITAIN AND NORTHERN IRELAND: NOTIFICATION UNDER ARTICLE 45 (4)}}</ref>
